\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {22}{\ignorespaces Sensitivity of the final configuration: each arm, refitted with one setting changed, as its move from the final configuration in units of the final configuration's standard deviation over its three seeds, per readout: held-out reconstruction, NMI, mirror $R^2$, the response's information about the niche, the nonlinear probe's composition share, and the transport fraction of the ceiling (trusted tier; on the TMA core over the seeds with a trusted panel). Shaded: $\pm 2$ standard deviations; filled points lie outside it. Arrows point toward the better direction, the side of zero on which a move is an improvement. Moves beyond five standard deviations carry their value; the axis is wide enough to show the largest, the fixed false-positive floor's transport move on the primary section. The arms' values are in \cref  {tab:sensitivity}.\relax }}{57}{figure.caption.129}\protected@file@percent }
