\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {24}{\ignorespaces The planted per-cell response against its strength $s$. \textbf  {a},\nobreakspace  {}KL AUC separating the planted cells from the other cells of their type by their response divergence; \textbf  {b},\nobreakspace  {}absorption of the plant by the intrinsic latent, read through the decoder along the planted direction; \textbf  {c},\nobreakspace  {}the Spearman correlation of the per-cell divergence between seeds. World 0, on which the rule fixed in advance decides, in bold; worlds 1 and 2, replications, lighter. Points: mean over three model seeds (seed pairs in c); bars: their range. Dashed: the rule's detection thresholds, a KL AUC of at least $0.8$ in every seed and a Spearman correlation of at least $0.5$ in every seed pair. Arrows point toward the better direction; absorption and the agreement between seeds have none. The values are in \cref  {tab:planted-percell}.\relax }}{61}{figure.caption.143}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:planted-percell}{{24}{61}{The planted per-cell response against its strength $s$. \textbf {a},~KL AUC separating the planted cells from the other cells of their type by their response divergence; \textbf {b},~absorption of the plant by the intrinsic latent, read through the decoder along the planted direction; \textbf {c},~the Spearman correlation of the per-cell divergence between seeds. World 0, on which the rule fixed in advance decides, in bold; worlds 1 and 2, replications, lighter. Points: mean over three model seeds (seed pairs in c); bars: their range. Dashed: the rule's detection thresholds, a KL AUC of at least $0.8$ in every seed and a Spearman correlation of at least $0.5$ in every seed pair. Arrows point toward the better direction; absorption and the agreement between seeds have none. The values are in \cref {tab:planted-percell}.\relax }{figure.caption.143}{}}
